WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.080
This video covers section locks.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.950
noctune drafts the note
as one card per section.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.950
Each card has its own buttons
to edit, lock, or regenerate it.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.910
Review the draft against the
recording before you change anything.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.910
To fix one section,
choose Edit on its card.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.560
The recording says her
weight is up a touch,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.230
so change stable to up
slightly, and choose Save.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.360
The section locks
automatically, and its label

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.590
shows who edited it, and when.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.800
Locked sections have no
Regenerate button, so

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.590
new recordings and
regenerations can't change them.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.310
On an unlocked section, choose Regenerate,
and add an instruction if you like.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.430
noctune shows the rewrite
before anything changes.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.325
Removed text is crossed out,
and new lines are highlighted.

00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:48.685
Choose Apply rewrite, and
that section locks too.

00:00:48.775 --> 00:00:50.845
Or choose Discard to leave it as it was.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.530
Practice templates are locked too.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.650
Owners and admins edit them
and set the practice default.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.185
Everyone else can use them,
set one as their default, or

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:03.055
duplicate it to My templates
to make their own version.

00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:05.705
Locks protect your
reviewed work, but every

00:01:05.705 --> 00:01:07.615
note still needs your clinical review.
